From ea2e58ef24388ea2341c5a9e747bf757d37709ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 15:52:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix Pile-On Configure to a real dropdown, remove Win-Back's
 slider, transparency sweep
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Pile-On Configure was opening EnablePileOnModal — a centered modal with
an Enable/Ask-Teammates tab switcher built for the Library's first-time
enable flow, not a settings dropdown. Worse, if a viewer's browser had
previously landed on the "Ask Teammates" tab for ANY worker (the mode
is remembered globally, not per-worker), Configure would open straight
into a live chat that auto-sends "Update Pile-On settings for X" on
mount (TeammatesChat's initialPendingMessage really does call send()
immediately, not just prefill a draft). Replaced with the same pattern
every other skill's Configure already uses: SkillConfigureMenu's
FloatingPanel dropdown + a plain two-field form (pile-on-config-form.tsx,
new) — no modal, no chat, ever. Reverted the configureMode additions to
EnablePileOnModal from the previous commit since nothing uses that path
anymore; deleted the now-redundant pile-on-configure-button.tsx.

win-back-view.tsx:
- The touchpoint preview opened a slide-over Sheet drawer for every
  email/SMS in the cadence — removed entirely in favor of expanding the
  message body inline below its row (same pattern win-back-cadence-
  preview.tsx already uses), copy button and all.
- The enrollment banner showed prospectName ?? prospectEmail — only
  ever one or the other. Now shows both together when both exist.

engagements/[id]/page.tsx: Runtime Ownership panel was still
no-ambient-glow surface-glass-1 — swept to transparent + border like
everywhere else this session.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AkznvRLnBokzbdmJ2WwaEM
